# Final Recommendation

## Master These First

### Tier 1 (Core Deep Learning)
- Neural Networks
- Forward & Backpropagation
- Gradient Descent
- Loss Functions
- Activation Functions
- Optimizers
- Learning Rate Scheduling
- Dropout
- BatchNorm
- LayerNorm
- Weight Initialization
- Vanishing/Exploding Gradients
- Gradient Clipping

### Tier 2 (Computer Vision + NLP + Transformers)
- CNN
- Pooling
- Padding
- Stride
- RNN
- LSTM
- GRU
- Attention
- Self-Attention
- Multi-Head Attention
- Positional Encoding
- Transformer
- Decoder-only GPT
- Embeddings
- Tokenization
- Text Generation

### Tier 3 (Project-Oriented Topics)
- Transfer Learning
- Fine-tuning
- LoRA/QLoRA
- RAG
- FAISS/ChromaDB
- Prompt Engineering
- Perplexity & Evaluation
- Mixed Precision
- Quantization

For **AI/ML Fresher interviews**, focus on **Tier 1 + Tier 2**. If your resume includes projects like **MiniGPT** or **Research Paper RAG**, you should also master the relevant **Tier 3** topics, as interviewers commonly ask follow-up questions based on your implementation.
